# open: `merl` in a service repository, the first minute. The tree lists what .gitignore leaves
# out, dim (.venv, .env); o opens a file by a few letters of its name; / finds whatever the case
# (#5) and n moves on; : jumps to a line; t hides the tree; ? lists the keys; q gives the shell
# back: merl's screen gone, exit status 0.
merl
# the welcome screen beside the tree
wait Open a file (fuzzy)
key o
type uow
key Enter
wait app/uow.py  1:1  [code]
# `db` found for DB, seven of them, and n to the second
key /
type DB
wait 1/7
key Enter n
wait app/uow.py  8:14  [code]  2/7
key :
type 15
key Enter
wait app/uow.py  15:1
# the tree hidden, the help over the code
key t ?
wait Go to definition of the word under the cursor
key Escape q
wait merl exited: 0
